SELECT class 
FROM courses
WHERE COUNT(*) >= 5
GROUP BY class; is wrong bcs 
COUNT() is an aggregate function, and aggregate functions cannot be used in the WHERE clause.

SQL execution order explains why.

SQL execution order

FROM

WHERE

GROUP BY

HAVING

SELECT

So when WHERE runs, the grouping has not happened yet, therefore COUNT() does not exist yet.
WHERE filters rows before grouping

HAVING filters groups after aggregation
